###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - No training or test errors are stated in the main text; the ML force statistical error ('about 80 meV/A', SM) reflects DMC noise. Hyperparameters are in the SM (not read).
# - The Delta-DMC model is a residual fit on top of Delta-DFT rather than a fine-tune of its weights; base_model relation 'fine-tuned' is the closest available and the label says so.
# - Phase diagram, equations of state, melting temperatures and structures are property results.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/niu2023.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.
